<title>SINGAPORE: TABLE - Meiban interim net falls 18 pct.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Meiban interim net falls 18 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1997</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			    1.52   vs    1.86</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		   1.76   vs    3.02</p>
<p>    Turnover			     12.42   vs   19.61</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest     0.05   vs    0.11</p>
<p>    Depreciation and amortisation   0.47   vs    0.53</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			2.02   vs    2.49</p>
<p>    Profits from associates	   0.05   vs    0.21</p>
<p>    Tax				     0.54   vs    0.84</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries		     0.11   vs    nil</p>
<p>Note - Meiban Plastic Ltd said it expected to improve its performance in the second half of 1997 based on increased production capacity at its new plant and an expected recovery in the electronics industry.</p>
